sentences.l:
So long as we go through the fields and the works of men,
so long with the attendants after the mules and the wagon
quickly go;

But when we set foot on the city, around which is a tower
high, and fair a harbour on either side of the city,
and narrow the entrance;

But when the house and the court have hidden you within,
very swiftly through the hall to go, until you reach
my mother;

and she sits at the hearth in the firelight,
turning sea-purple yarn, a wonder to see,
leaning against a pillar;
